    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d70">

                <pb facs="0165" n="63" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg63"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4 Personnel/1464: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Delegate</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-09-03T19:00:00-04:00">September 3,
                            1935—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>500. Your 1054, September 2, 6 p.m. You are instructed to release quarters now
                    occupied by Disarmament Delegation about first of October or upon termination of
                    next Bureau meeting, unless in your judgment the situation subsequent to that
                    date would require you to maintain the office for a brief period longer.
                    Quarters will be obtained in building occupied by Consulate.<anchor n="92"
                        xml:id="d70-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d70-f1" n="92" xml:id="d70-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 1062, October 30, 1935, noon, the American delegate reported the
                    change of office had been effected (500.A15A4 Personnel/1488).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
